 "answer_raw": "Amazon has a localized presence in **Brazil** and **Mexico** within the South American/Latin American region, but it does not have dedicated marketplaces in most other South American countries [4].\n\nWhile the company has established storefronts in several major economies, the existing dataset shows that **Brazil** and **Mexico** are the primary countries with dedicated Amazon marketplaces in that part of the world [4]. For other countries without their own dedicated storefronts, residents can often still access products through **international shipping** to their specific locations [4].\n\nI didn't find specific competitors or the primary alternatives people use in other South American countries; you would need to check local e-commerce market share reports or regional retail leaders to identify those alternatives.",
